<title>USA: Fannie Mae issues $250 mln preferred stock.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae issues $250 mln preferred stock.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal National Mortgage Association Tuesday said it issued $250 million of preferred stock, or five million shares of 6.45 percent preferred stock with a stated value of $50 per share.</p>
<p>Fannie Mae said this is the third and final issue of preferred stock under a capital restructuring program it announced last December.</p>
<p>It said that with today's issue, it has issued $1 billion of preferred stock this year.</p>
</text>
